{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>The first of the first fruits.</b> Why is it said? Since it is stated: 'And you shall take of the first of the fruit of the ground' — I have only produce; liquids, from where do I know? Scripture says: 'you shall bring,' in any case. And what is the difference between these and those? These — one brings and recites, and those — one brings and does not recite. It mentioned it after 'do not slaughter upon leaven,' since from Pesah the first fruits begin." "<b>You shall not cook a kid in its mother's milk.</b> Since on the festival one eats many animals, he warned in the passage of festivals not to cook and not to eat a kid in its mother's milk." "<b>[</b> Another interpretation: for it is a way of gluttony and cruelty.]" "<b>[You shall not cook</b> — an expression of preparing food and making ready.]"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:05.620687123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}